<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Regreg War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1404–1406</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Regreg War was a civil war in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/majapahit-empire">Majapahit</a> kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a>, fought from 1404 to 1406 between the western court of King Wikramawardhana and the eastern court of Bhre Wirabhumi, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hayam-wuruk">Hayam Wuruk</a>. Wirabhumi was defeated and killed, but the war weakened Majapahit's hold over its overseas dependencies, and envoys of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zheng-he">Zheng He</a>'s Chinese fleet were killed in the fighting.</p></div>
